{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For no man shall see Me and live.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): that he would live — and this is what is mentioned in the matter of Manoah (Judges 13:22): ״מות נמות כי אלהים ראינו״ — 'we shall surely die, for we have seen Elohim.' And if regarding the sight of an angel Scripture says thus, all the more regarding the sight of the Blessed Name, that he would not survive the vision, for his soul would separate from him; but after his death he does see. And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: 'in their lifetime they do not see, but at the time of their death they do see.' And likewise it says (Psalms 22:30): ״לפניו יכרעו כל יורדי עפר״. And so we find regarding Rabbi Abbahu, that he saw his reward close to his death and said: ״כל אלין לאבהו״ — 'all these are for Abbahu.'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: ״כי לא יראני האדם״ — He did not say ״כי לא יראה אותי״, because this prevention is not from HaShem, for behold it is written in Isaiah (Isaiah 6): ״ואראה את ה׳״, and likewise (Exodus 24:10): ״ויראו את אלהי ישראל״ — for he did not say ״ויראו אלהי ישראל״, but he added the את, as I explained there. And it is what Ezekiel said (Ezekiel 2:2): ״ואשמע את מדבר אלי״, and likewise (Psalms 145:20): ״ואת כל הרשעים ישמיד״ — for the attribute of mercy guards all who love Him, and the attribute of judgment destroys the wicked. And He mentioned האדם with the definite article, for according to the plain sense Scripture ought to have said ״כי לא יראה אותי אדם וחי״; but Scripture clarifies that the prevention applies only to His essence and the reality of the Name that is uniquely His, and even for the man inscribed with the life of the Chariot. This is the explanation of ״כי לא יראני האדם וחי״." "<b>And this is</b> what they said in the Midrash: ״כי לא יראני האדם וחי״ — Rabbi Akiva says: even the חיות הנושאות (the living creatures that bear [the Chariot]) do not see the Glory. Rabbi Shimon ben Yochai says: even the ministering angels, whose lives are eternal life, do not see the Glory."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "The phrase הש\"י resolved as 'the Blessed Name' based on context; the trailing phrase 'this is the explanation of...' closes the comment without a dangling colon in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:53.763089263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}